# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Las técnicas de
# mitigación de errores [PEA](/guides/error-mi
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"The error mitigation techniques [PEA](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#pea) and [PEC](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#pec) both utilize a noise learning component based on a [Pauli-Lindblad noise model](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866), which is typically managed during execution after submitting one or more jobs through `qiskit-ibm-runtime` without any local access to the fitted noise model. However, as of `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.27.1, a [`NoiseLearner`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/noise-learner) and associated  [`NoiseLearnerOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-noise-learner-options) class have been created to obtain the results of these noise learning experiments. These results can then be stored locally as a `NoiseLearnerResult` and used as input in later experiments. This page provides an overview of its usage and the associated options available.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition, starting with `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.47.0, there is a new "
"`NoiseLearnerV3` class that is compatible with the Executor primitive. This "
"new version, also part of the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-"
"execution-model), gives you the ability to explicitly specify the layers you"
" want to learn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Además, a partir de `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.47.0, existe una nueva clase "
"`NoiseLearnerV3` compatible con la primitiva Executor. Esta nueva versión, "
"también parte del [modelo de ejecución dirigida](/guides/directed-execution-"
"model), te permite especificar explícitamente las capas que deseas "
"aprender.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"`NoiseLearner` only works with EstimatorV2 and `NoiseLearnerV3` only works with Executor.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"`NoiseLearner` solo funciona con EstimatorV2 y `NoiseLearnerV3` solo funciona con Executor.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`NoiseLearner` {#noiselearner}"
msgstr "`NoiseLearner` {#noiselearner}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Descripción general {#overview}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `NoiseLearner` class performs experiments that characterize noise "
"processes based on a Pauli-Lindblad noise model for one (or more) circuits. "
"It possesses a `run()` method that executes the learning experiments and "
"takes as input either a list of circuits or a [PUB](/guides/primitive-input-"
"output), and returns a `NoiseLearnerResult` containing the learned noise "
"channels and metadata about the job(s) submitted. Below is a code snippet "
"demonstrating the usage of the helper program.\n"
msgstr ""
"La clase `NoiseLearner` realiza experimentos que caracterizan los procesos "
"de ruido basándose en un modelo de ruido de Pauli-Lindblad para uno o más "
"circuitos. Dispone de un método `run()` que ejecuta los experimentos de "
"aprendizaje y acepta como entrada una lista de circuitos o un "
"[PUB](/guides/primitive-input-output); devuelve un `NoiseLearnerResult` que "
"contiene los canales de ruido aprendidos y metadatos sobre los trabajos "
"enviados. A continuación se muestra un fragmento de código que demuestra el "
"uso del programa asistente.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The resulting `NoiseLearnerResult.data` is a list of "
"[`LayerError`](../api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/utils-noise-learner-result-layer-"
"error) objects containing the [noise "
"model](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866) for each individual entangling "
"layer that belongs to the target circuit(s). Each `LayerError` stores the "
"layer information, in the form of a circuit and a set of qubit labels, "
"alongside the [`PauliLindbladError`](../api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/utils-noise-"
"learner-result-pauli-lindblad-error) for the noise model that was learned "
"for the given layer.\n"
msgstr ""
"El `NoiseLearnerResult.data` resultante es una lista de objetos "
"[`LayerError`](../api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/utils-noise-learner-result-layer-"
"error) que contienen el [modelo de ruido](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866) "
"para cada capa de entrelazamiento individual que pertenece a los circuitos "
"objetivo. Cada `LayerError` almacena la información de la capa, en forma de "
"circuito y un conjunto de etiquetas de qubits, junto con el "
"[`PauliLindbladError`](../api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/utils-noise-learner-result-"
"pauli-lindblad-error) para el modelo de ruido aprendido para la capa dada.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `LayerError.error` attribute of the noise learning result contains the "
"generators and error rates of the fitted Pauli Lindblad model, which has the"
" form\n"
msgstr ""
"El atributo `LayerError.error` del resultado del aprendizaje de ruido "
"contiene los generadores y las tasas de error del modelo de Pauli-Lindblad "
"ajustado, que tiene la forma\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$ \\Lambda(\\rho) = \\exp{\\sum_j r_j \\left(P_j \\rho P_j^\\dagger - "
"\\rho\\right)}, $$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$ \\Lambda(\\rho) = \\exp{\\sum_j r_j \\left(P_j \\rho P_j^\\dagger - "
"\\rho\\right)}, $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the $r_j$ are the `LayerError.rates` and $P_j$ are the Pauli operators"
" specified in `LayerError.generators`.\n"
msgstr ""
"donde los $r_j$ son los `LayerError.rates` y los $P_j$ son los operadores de"
" Pauli especificados en `LayerError.generators`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Noise learning options {#noise-learning-options}"
msgstr "Opciones de aprendizaje de ruido {#noise-learning-options}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can choose among several options to input when you instantiate a "
"`NoiseLearner` object. These options are encapsulated by the "
"`qiskit_ibm_runtime.options.NoiseLearnerOptions` class and include the "
"ability to specify the maximum layers to learn, number of randomizations, "
"and the twirling strategy, among others. Refer to the "
"[`NoiseLearnerOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options-noise-learner-options) API documentation for detailed "
"information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Puedes elegir entre varias opciones al instanciar un objeto `NoiseLearner`. "
"Estas opciones están encapsuladas por la clase "
"`qiskit_ibm_runtime.options.NoiseLearnerOptions` e incluyen la posibilidad "
"de especificar el número máximo de capas a aprender, el número de "
"aleatorizaciones y la estrategia de twirling, entre otras. Consulta la "
"documentación de la API de "
"[`NoiseLearnerOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options-noise-learner-options) para obtener información detallada.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following is a simple example that shows how to use the "
"`NoiseLearnerOptions` in a `NoiseLearner` experiment:\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación se muestra un ejemplo sencillo que ilustra cómo usar "
"`NoiseLearnerOptions` en un experimento con `NoiseLearner`:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Input noise model to a primitive {#input-noise-model-to-a-primitive}"
msgstr ""
"Pasar el modelo de ruido a una primitiva {#input-noise-model-to-a-primitive}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The noise model learned on the circuit can also be used as an input to the "
"`EstimatorV2` primitive implemented in Qiskit Runtime. This can be passed "
"into the primitive a few different ways. The next three examples show how "
"you can pass the noise model to the `estimator.options` attribute directly, "
"by using a `ResilienceOptionsV2` object before instantiating an Estimator "
"primitive, and by passing in an appropriately formatted dictionary.\n"
msgstr ""
"El modelo de ruido aprendido sobre el circuito también puede usarse como "
"entrada para la primitiva `EstimatorV2` implementada en Qiskit Runtime. Este"
" puede pasarse a la primitiva de varias formas distintas. Los siguientes "
"tres ejemplos muestran cómo puedes pasar el modelo de ruido al atributo "
"`estimator.options` directamente, usando un objeto `ResilienceOptionsV2` "
"antes de instanciar una primitiva Estimator, y pasando un diccionario con el"
" formato adecuado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After the noise model is passed into the `EstimatorV2` object, it can be "
"used to run workloads and perform error mitigation as normal.\n"
msgstr ""
"Después de pasar el modelo de ruido al objeto `EstimatorV2`, puede usarse "
"para ejecutar cargas de trabajo y realizar la mitigación de errores de forma"
" normal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"
msgstr "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview-1}"
msgstr "Descripción general {#overview-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to `NoiseLearner`, the `NoiseLearnerV3` class performs experiments "
"that characterize noise processes based on a Pauli-Lindblad noise model for "
"one or more circuits. Its `run()` method takes a list of instructions, each "
"of which must be a twirled-annotated "
"[`BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp) "
"containing [ISA](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) "
"operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"De manera similar a `NoiseLearner`, la clase `NoiseLearnerV3` realiza "
"experimentos que caracterizan los procesos de ruido basándose en un modelo "
"de ruido de Pauli-Lindblad para uno o más circuitos. Su método `run()` "
"acepta una lista de instrucciones, cada una de las cuales debe ser un "
"[`BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp) con "
"anotaciones de twirling que contenga operaciones "
"[ISA](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The result of a `NoiseLearnerV3` job contains a list of [`NoiseLearnerV3Result`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-v3-result) objects, one for each input instruction.\n"
"The following code shows how to use the helper program.\n"
msgstr ""
"El resultado de un trabajo `NoiseLearnerV3` contiene una lista de objetos [`NoiseLearnerV3Result`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-v3-result), uno por cada instrucción de entrada.\n"
"El siguiente código muestra cómo usar el programa asistente.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The job result is a list of `NoiseLearnerV3Result` objects, one for each "
"input-boxed set of instructions. `NoiseLearnerV3Result` has a "
"`to_pauli_lindblad_map()` method that returns a "
"[`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap)"
" object, which has methods to extract the generators, error rates, and "
"more.\n"
msgstr ""
"El resultado del trabajo es una lista de objetos `NoiseLearnerV3Result`, uno"
" por cada conjunto de instrucciones encuadradas de entrada. "
"`NoiseLearnerV3Result` tiene un método `to_pauli_lindblad_map()` que "
"devuelve un objeto "
"[`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap),"
" el cual tiene métodos para extraer los generadores, las tasas de error y "
"más.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Noise learning options {#noise-learning-options-1}"
msgstr "Opciones de aprendizaje de ruido {#noise-learning-options-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NoiseLearnerV3` supports several options, including the number of "
"randomizations and layer pair depth, among others. Similar to the "
"primitives, you can specify the options during or after instantiating the "
"`NoiseLearnerV3` object. The previous code example  demonstrated how to set "
"the  `shots_per_randomization` and `num_randomizations` options. Refer to "
"the [`NoiseLearnerV3Options`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options-models-noise-learner-v3-options) API documentation for "
"detailed information.\n"
msgstr ""
"`NoiseLearnerV3` admite varias opciones, incluido el número de "
"aleatorizaciones y la profundidad de pares de capas, entre otras. De manera "
"similar a las primitivas, puedes especificar las opciones durante o después "
"de instanciar el objeto `NoiseLearnerV3`. El ejemplo de código anterior "
"muestra cómo establecer las opciones `shots_per_randomization` y "
"`num_randomizations`. Consulta la documentación de la API de "
"[`NoiseLearnerV3Options`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options-models-noise-learner-v3-options) para obtener información "
"detallada.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Input a noise model to Executor {#input-a-noise-model-to-executor}"
msgstr ""
"Pasar un modelo de ruido a Executor {#input-a-noise-model-to-executor}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Executor follows the design intents specified in circuit annotations (in the"
" form of a samplex) and options. `InjectNoise` is the annotation for "
"specifying where to inject noise, and the `pauli_lindblad_maps` samplex "
"argument specifies which noise map to use.\n"
msgstr ""
"Executor sigue los objetivos de diseño especificados en las anotaciones del "
"circuito (en forma de samplex) y las opciones. `InjectNoise` es la anotación"
" para especificar dónde inyectar el ruido, y el argumento "
"`pauli_lindblad_maps` del samplex especifica qué mapa de ruido usar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit in the previous example runs through the boxing pass manager, which groups instructions into annotated boxes. The relevant code is added here for ease of understanding.\n"
"- `inject_noise_targets=”gates”` specifies to add the `InjectNoise` annotations to boxes that contain entanglers.\n"
"- `inject_noise_strategy=\"uniform_modification\"` specifies to assign the same `ref` and `modifier_ref` to all equivalent boxes with `InjectNoise` annotations.\n"
"      - `InjectNoise.ref` is a unique identifier used to assign a noise model to that box.\n"
"      - `InjectNoise.modifier_ref` allows scaling the noise model assigned to a box by multiplicative factors.\n"
msgstr ""
"El circuito del ejemplo anterior se procesa mediante el boxing pass manager, que agrupa las instrucciones en cajas anotadas. El código relevante se incluye aquí para facilitar la comprensión.\n"
"- `inject_noise_targets=\"gates\"` especifica que se añadan las anotaciones `InjectNoise` a las cajas que contienen operaciones de entrelazamiento.\n"
"- `inject_noise_strategy=\"uniform_modification\"` especifica que se asigne el mismo `ref` y `modifier_ref` a todas las cajas equivalentes con anotaciones `InjectNoise`.\n"
"      - `InjectNoise.ref` es un identificador único que se usa para asignar un modelo de ruido a esa caja.\n"
"      - `InjectNoise.modifier_ref` permite escalar el modelo de ruido asignado a una caja mediante factores multiplicativos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit from the previous example contains three boxes, two of which "
"contain `InjectNoise` annotations with different `ref` attributes (since "
"they are not equivalent).\n"
msgstr ""
"El circuito del ejemplo anterior contiene tres cajas, dos de las cuales "
"tienen anotaciones `InjectNoise` con atributos `ref` diferentes (ya que no "
"son equivalentes).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The result of the `NoiseLearnerV3` job must be converted to a dictionary "
"before being passed to Executor. This dictionary's keys are the "
"`InjectNoise.ref` attributes and the values are the corresponding noise "
"maps. This mapping tells Executor which noise models to inject where.\n"
msgstr ""
"El resultado del trabajo `NoiseLearnerV3` debe convertirse en un diccionario"
" antes de pasarse a Executor. Las claves de este diccionario son los "
"atributos `InjectNoise.ref` y los valores son los mapas de ruido "
"correspondientes. Este mapeo le indica a Executor qué modelos de ruido "
"inyectar y dónde.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code shows how to take the circuit and the `NoiseLearnerV3` "
"result from the previous example and pass them to Executor, which will "
"generate the circuit variants with the injected noise models and execute "
"them on hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"El siguiente código muestra cómo tomar el circuito y el resultado de "
"`NoiseLearnerV3` del ejemplo anterior y pasarlos a Executor, que generará "
"las variantes del circuito con los modelos de ruido inyectados y las "
"ejecutará en hardware.\n"

